# =============================================
# OrchestAI — Environment Variables (Example)
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values
# =============================================

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────
# Use the exact user/password you created in PostgreSQL
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/orchestai_db

# ─── Redis (optional for MVP) ────────────────
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# ─── Authentication ──────────────────────────
# Change this secret for any production use!
JWT_SECRET=change-this-to-a-long-random-string
JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=60
JWT_REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRE_DAYS=30

# ─── AI / OpenAI ─────────────────────────────
# Leave blank to use AI Mock Mode (no API cost)
OPENAI_API_KEY=IMPORTANT DEVELOPMENT REQUIREMENTS

This project will primarily run on localhost during development and demo presentations.

The main priority is:
- Fast local setup
- Smooth localhost execution
- Stable UI/UX
- Easy database connection
- Simple startup commands
- Minimal deployment complexity

Deployment is secondary.

==================================================
LOCAL DEVELOPMENT PRIORITY
==================================================

Optimize the entire architecture for localhost development first.

Requirements:
- One-command startup
- Simple environment setup
- Minimal configuration
- Fast refresh
- Easy debugging
- Stable PostgreSQL connection
- No Kubernetes
- No microservices complexity initially
- Avoid unnecessary cloud architecture
- Keep MVP modular but simple

==================================================
LOCALHOST STACK REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

Frontend:
- Next.js
- TailwindCSS
- shadcn/ui
- React Flow

Backend:
- FastAPI

Database:
- PostgreSQL running locally

Cache/Queue:
- Redis optional only if required

==================================================
RUNNING REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

The AI should generate setup so the project can run locally using:

Frontend:
npm install
npm run dev

Backend:
pip install -r requirements.txt
uvicorn app.main:app --reload

Database:
PostgreSQL local instance

==================================================
DOCKER REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

Docker should be OPTIONAL.

Do NOT make Docker mandatory for development.

Generate:
- Normal localhost setup
- Optional Docker setup

==================================================
POSTGRESQL REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

Use local PostgreSQL configuration.

Example:
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/ai_workforce_db

Generate:
- SQL schema
- Seed scripts
- Auto table creation
- Alembic migrations

==================================================
VERCEL DEPLOYMENT REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

Frontend deployment target:
- Vercel

Backend deployment:
- Optional later
- Keep backend easily deployable

Do NOT over-engineer deployment.

==================================================
SIMPLIFIED ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

Use a clean monolithic modular architecture initially.

Structure:

frontend/
backend/
database/
docs/

Avoid:
- Complex distributed systems
- Kubernetes
- Kafka
- Over-engineered event systems

==================================================
MVP PRIORITY FEATURES
==================================================

Build these first:

1. Authentication
2. Dashboard
3. Employee management
4. Project management
5. DAG workflow visualization
6. AI team recommendation
7. Task tracking
8. PostgreSQL integration
9. POS management
10. Analytics dashboard

==================================================
UI PRIORITY
==================================================

The localhost demo should look visually impressive.

Focus heavily on:
- Dashboard UI
- Smooth animations
- Enterprise SaaS feel
- Modern cards/charts
- DAG workflow visuals
- Responsive design

==================================================
DEVELOPMENT EXPERIENCE
==================================================

Generate:
- Simple folder structure
- Clear comments
- Easy setup guide
- Beginner-friendly commands
- Minimal environment variables
- Fast local startup

==================================================
GENERATE THESE FILES
==================================================

- README.md
- SETUP_GUIDE.md
- .env.example
- requirements.txt
- package.json
- docker-compose.yml (optional)
- seed_data.py
- init_db.sql

==================================================
FINAL REQUIREMENT
==================================================

The project should:
- Run perfectly on localhost
- Be easy to demonstrate in hackathons
- Be easy to debug
- Be visually impressive
- Use PostgreSQL locally
- Be easy to later deploy on Vercel
- Avoid unnecessary production complexity initially
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# Set true to skip real OpenAI calls during local dev
AI_MOCK_MODE=true

# ─── Frontend ────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8000

# ─── App Settings ────────────────────────────
APP_NAME=OrchestAI
APP_ENV=development
APP_DEBUG=true
APP_HOST=0.0.0.0
APP_PORT=8000
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:3001

# ─── Email (optional for local) ──────────────
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
SMTP_FROM=noreply@orchestai.com

# ─── Celery (optional — only if using background jobs) ────
CELERY_BROKER_URL=redis://localhost:6379/1
CELERY_RESULT_BACKEND=redis://localhost:6379/2

# ─── OAuth (optional) ────────────────────────
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ─── Slack / Teams (optional) ────────────────
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
TEAMS_WEBHOOK_URL=
